1
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,000
King of the Bingo Game is a drama film directed by Elise Robertson.

2
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Harlem, 1943.

3
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Sonny is a struggling African American who frequents the bingo parlor in a desperate
attempt to provide for his family in post-Depression era New York.

4
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Sonny, played by Colman Domingo.

5
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:46,000
George, played by Bennie Lewis.

6
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Leroy, played by Earl L. Robertson.

7
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Woman Eating Peanuts, played by Rashida Clendening.

8
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Film Noir Hero, played by Peter Macon.

9
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Film Noir Female, played by Anika Noni Rose.

10
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Richard Karn (born Richard Karn Wilson; February 17, 1956) is an
American actor, author and former game show host.

11
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:10,000
He starred as Al Borland in the ABC series Home Improvement
and as Fred Peters in the Hulu series Pen15.

12
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Karn was also the fourth host of Family Feud from 2002 to 2006.

13
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:38,000
The film explores themes of bingo, racism, harlem,
new york city, 1940s, anti-blackness.

14
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:22,000
The tone is emotional.
